From a1d68ac9e7f7b7118f0fa04b3fc3c807b321cca8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oneshot <oneshot@localhost>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:46:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] 0032: Bedrock touch, part 2

- floating left stick that goes away with the finger; sprint by pushing it
  to the rim, the sprint button hidden in the Bedrock preset (layout rev 2)
- repeated hits while a finger holds on a mob, at the weapon's cooldown
- shield in the off hand beside a sword, axe or empty hand: raised by a hold
  on nothing or while sneaking (Bedrock); a hold on a mob hits, on a block breaks
- the camera turns while drawing a bow, crossbow, trident or spyglass, and the
  crosshair shows; a brush still acts under the finger
- slot screens: a tap moves a stack across (shift-click), a hold takes it
  into the hand, a drag carries it and puts it down where the finger lifts
  (a swapped stack goes back to the drag's start), no more one-by-one
  spreading; a tap on the creative grid gives a stack (never the locked
  placeholder), a vertical swipe there scrolls; nothing is clicked once the
  screen under the finger is gone

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
